{"text": "2074163213\n\nFrom: MBUCKING--VCHOO21A Date and time 25.06.97 17:03:38\nTo: Distribution\n\nFrom: Kathleen Linehan\nTo: Distribution\nSubject: Corporate Affairs Weekly Highlights, week ending 25.04.97\n\nCENTRAL EUROPE\nCZECH REPUBLIC\nProduct Tssues\n\n\u2018The Ministry of Industry and Trade published further information\nregarding the Czech government's decision to impose an Inport Deposit\nsystem as a measure to xestrain the growing trade deficit. the\ndeposit has been fixed at 20% of the invoice value, blocked for 180\ndays from the date of importation. Effective as of April 21, this\nsystem will apply to all imports of consuner goods, including\ncigarettes and tobacco in any form. Raw materials imported for re-\nexport as finished products to countries other than Slovakia are\nexempt. Area is appealing to the Czech Ministry of Agriculture to\ninclude raw tobacco in the list of exempt products.\n\nHUNGARY\nConsumer Issues\n\nIn a meeting of the Occupational Safety and Health Committee of the\nNational Interest Reconciliation Boar\u00e9, employers associations\nrepresented at the meeting unanimously rejected che anti~snoking\nlegislation prepared by the Ministry of Health. The Trade Union\nrepresentatives also rejected the imposition of employee fines and\nrequested further discussion. The employers associations submitted a\njoint written position to the Ministry of Health, the Ministry of\nLabor and to the Prime Minister's office.\n\nMIDDLE EAST / ARICA\n\u2018goRDAN\nProduct Issues .\n\nInternational and local cigarette manufacturers participated in the\nsecond neeting held at the Jordanian Institute of Standards and\nMetrology to continue discussions relating to proposed amendments to\nJordan's standard specification for cigarettes. Some progress was\nmade and another meeting was set for May 10. It was evident from\ndiscussions with the Ministry of Health representative after the\nmeeting that the ministry is insisting on a proposed reduction in\nMcLs to 12 and 1 as a condition to show any flexibility on other\nLimits to technical parameters contained in the draft.\n\nEASTERN EUROPE -", "words": [{"text": "2074163213", "x0": 473, "y0": 71, "x1": 598, "y1": 91, "conf": 51.0}, {"text": "From:", "x0": 100, "y0": 114, "x1": 127, "y1": 121, "conf": 71.0}, {"text": "MBUCKING--VCHOO21A", "x0": 141, "y0": 114, "x1": 263, "y1": 121, "conf": 56.0}, {"text": "Date", "x0": 397, "y0": 115, "x1": 423, "y1": 122, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "and", "x0": 430, "y0": 115, "x1": 450, "y1": 122, "conf": 91.0}, {"text": "time", "x0": 458, "y0": 116, "x1": 483, "y1": 122, "conf": 85.0}, {"text": "25.06.97", "x0": 511, "y0": 115, "x1": 563, "y1": 123, "conf": 55.0}, {"text": "17:03:38", "x0": 572, "y0": 116, "x1": 624, "y1": 123, "conf": 92.0}, {"text": "To:", "x0": 100, "y0": 128, "x1": 118, "y1": 135, "conf": 76.0}, {"text": "Distribution", "x0": 127, "y0": 127, "x1": 208, "y1": 136, "conf": 83.0}, {"text": "From:", "x0": 100, "y0": 157, "x1": 131, "y1": 164, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "Kathleen", "x0": 141, "y0": 156, "x1": 195, "y1": 164, "conf": 87.0}, {"text": "Linehan", "x0": 202, "y0": 157, "x1": 249, "y1": 165, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "To:", "x0": 100, "y0": 172, "x1": 113, "y1": 179, "conf": 62.0}, {"text": "Distribution", "x0": 141, "y0": 170, "x1": 222, "y1": 179, "conf": 56.0}, {"text": "Subject:", "x0": 100, "y0": 185, "x1": 151, "y1": 195, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Corporate", "x0": 161, "y0": 186, "x1": 221, "y1": 195, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Affairs", "x0": 228, "y0": 186, "x1": 275, "y1": 194, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Weekly", "x0": 282, "y0": 186, "x1": 322, "y1": 196, "conf": 74.0}, {"text": "Highlights,", "x0": 329, "y0": 186, "x1": 400, "y1": 196, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "week", "x0": 409, "y0": 187, "x1": 436, "y1": 195, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "ending", "x0": 443, "y0": 187, "x1": 483, "y1": 197, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "25.04.97", "x0": 490, "y0": 187, "x1": 542, "y1": 195, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "CENTRAL", "x0": 